 "response": "Toris's budget is now **$2218K**.\n\n1. **Which records count.** Only Finance Office messages that change the budget count. Messages from Marketing, the PMO, Sales, Vendor calls, Engineering, Legal, Operations and Facilities don't change it. Finance Office notes about audits, receipts, purchase orders and cost center codes don't either.\n2. **Withdrawals.** None of the records withdraws an earlier update, so every Finance Office budget change stays in effect.\n3. **Calculation.** The budget starts at $1710K (#0001). Applying every later increase and decrease in record order gives a running total along these lines:\n   - After the early changes up to #0050: about $2324K.\n   - Around #0400: $2436K.\n   - Around #0800: about $2257K.\n   - Around #1200: about $1788K.\n   - The last few changes: \u2212$110K (#1589) \u2192 $2273K; \u2212$115K (#1590) \u2192 $2273K; +$90K (#1591) \u2192 $2363K; +$100K (#1595) \u2192 $2463K; +$15K (#1596) \u2192 $2478K; \u2212$110K (#1597) \u2192 $2368K; \u2212$150K (#1600) \u2192 $2218K.\n\nThis is a hand-tallied running sum of several hundred changes, so a small slip in one step would carry through to the final figure.\n\nANSWER: $2218K",
